# Syluxium on the Linux kernel: busybox init (PID 1).
# rc.sysinit mounts everything, starts udev (hardware drivers) and the stick's
# log folder; then a root login shell on the first console, as before. With
# "desktop" on the kernel command line, that shell's profile starts the
# desktop (/etc/profile.d/zz-desktop.sh).
::sysinit:/usr/lib/syluxium/rc.sysinit
tty1::respawn:/usr/lib/syluxium/console-shell
tty2::askfirst:/usr/lib/syluxium/console-shell
::ctrlaltdel:/usr/bin/reboot
::shutdown:/usr/lib/syluxium/rc.shutdown
